    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d663-a1">

                <pb facs="1138" n="1038" xml:id="pg1038"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 77.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wheelock to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>66 <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Willow Street</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Brooklyn, N.
                                Y.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1880-07-10"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 10,
                    1880</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have just received word from Bolivar,
                    Venezuela, that Sotillo, the civil officer who committed the outrage upon me in
                    September last, has not been punished in any way, notwithstanding the assurances
                    of the President of the State before I left there that he should be
                    punished.</p>
                <p>Will you be kind enough to inform me whether the Venezuelan Government makes any
                    denial or justification of the outrage, as I have before reported to your
                    Department?</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>Very, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN E. WHEELOCK.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
